cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Creative Problem Solving: a divergence engine for open-ended problems"
message: "If you reference this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Golan
    given-names: Yaniv
    email: yaniv@golan.name
repository-code: "https://github.com/yaniv-golan/creative-problem-solving"
url: "https://github.com/yaniv-golan/creative-problem-solving"
abstract: >-
  An agent skill that generates non-obvious options for open-ended problems by running
  successive constrained passes, each refusing the move the last one made, rather than a
  single brainstorm. Built on the finding that branded creativity frameworks do not
  outperform a plain prompt with language models, while denial of the previous move,
  distribution sampling and self-category negation do. Publishes its eval definitions,
  graded results, full run transcripts, pre-registered experiment designs, and the rounds
  where the skill lost.
license: MIT
